javax.microedition.io.Connector.protocolpath: com.sun.midp.io
# v03.86: [gfx] drawing traces. NOT enabled here - this file is rebuilt from
# the app0 template on every round, so edits to the ux0: copy are thrown away,
# and app0: lives inside the VPK. To enable the traces, create this file:
#
#     ux0:/data/J2ME00001/gfx.cfg
#
# containing:
#
#     j2me.gfxdebug: 1
#     j2me.gfxbudget: 1200
#
# Its lines are appended to this property set verbatim. Each printed trace
# line costs ~26 ms of blocking flash I/O on the VM thread (the text is
# written twice: vm_output.log and vm_stderr.log, ~13 ms per small synchronous
# write to ux0:), so a title that draws 20-30 regions per frame will crawl
# while tracing - that is expected, not a regression. The budget is the TOTAL
# number of [gfx] lines per session. v03.90 raised the built-in default to 900
# because 极品飞车 emits ~77 lines per frame and 400 covered only two frames;
# omit the budget line entirely to get that default.
